ConfigMap Imperative Value:-

The ConfigMap can be created imperatively using the `kubectl create configmap` command. 
This command allows you to create a ConfigMap from literal values, files, or directories.

* kubectl create cm <name> --from-literal=<key>=<value>
* kubectl create cm <name> --from-literal=<Firatname>=chirag --from-literal=<lastvaluie>=rathi
* kubectl get cm 
* kubectl describe cm <name>
* kubectl create cm <name> --from-file=<path-to-file>
* kubectl create cm <name> --from-file=<path-to-directory>

declarative value:-
The ConfigMap can also be created declaratively using a YAML manifest file.
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: day19-configmap
data:
  user_name: Chirag
